{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Amulet</strong> is an indie action game about weaving through danger and quietly growing stronger.<br>You don\u2019t mash buttons. You don\u2019t juggle hotkeys. You <strong>point the mouse to move</strong>, and your attack fires automatically.<br>The fun lives in the <strong>dance</strong>: thread slow enemy projectiles, kite smartly, and feel your power ramp up.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As you defeat foes, you gain XP and <strong>auto-upgrade</strong>. No build menus mid-run. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Core Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Mouse-only movement:</strong> just point where to go. Combat happens automatically.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Readable bullet-hell:</strong> enemies fire <strong>slow, legible</strong> projectiles\u2014skill is in pathing and timing, not twitch spam.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Auto progression (no micromanage):</strong> XP \u2192 <strong>15 concise levels</strong>; multiple stats improve each ding.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Minimal HUD, maximum clarity:</strong> only the essentials; no mid-run menus or ability bars.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Short, satisfying runs:</strong> jump in, dance through danger, feel the ramp.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Design Pillars</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Purity:</strong> remove anything that doesn\u2019t make the core loop better.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Fairness:</strong> clear telegraphs, consistent rules, no cheap hits.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Feel:</strong> crunchy hits, juicy death animations, quick celebrations\u2014then back to the action.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you like games that are <strong>simple to play, hard to put down</strong>, Amulet aims right at that sweet spot: elegant input, readable challenge, and a steady sense of \u201cI\u2019m stronger than I was five minutes ago.\u201d</p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/2784910?t=1760564551","background_raw":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2784910/page_bg_raw.jpg?t=1760564551","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2784910/cc86e573e90d5b70f412541375ca29a05ef661d7/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1760564551","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2784910/cc86e573e90d5b70f412541375ca29a05ef661d7/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1760564551","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Amulet</strong> is an indie action game about weaving through danger and quietly growing stronger.<br>You don\u2019t mash buttons. You don\u2019t juggle hotkeys. You <strong>point the mouse to move</strong>, and your attack fires automatically.<br>The fun lives in the <strong>dance</strong>: thread slow enemy projectiles, kite smartly, and feel your power ramp up.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As you defeat foes, you gain XP and <strong>auto-upgrade</strong>. No build menus mid-run. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Core Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Mouse-only movement:</strong> just point where to go. Combat happens automatically.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Readable bullet-hell:</strong> enemies fire <strong>slow, legible</strong> projectiles\u2014skill is in pathing and timing, not twitch spam.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Auto progression (no micromanage):</strong> XP \u2192 <strong>15 concise levels</strong>; multiple stats improve each ding.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Minimal HUD, maximum clarity:</strong> only the essentials; no mid-run menus or ability bars.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Short, satisfying runs:</strong> jump in, dance through danger, feel the ramp.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Design Pillars</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Purity:</strong> remove anything that doesn\u2019t make the core loop better.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Fairness:</strong> clear telegraphs, consistent rules, no cheap hits.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Feel:</strong> crunchy hits, juicy death animations, quick celebrations\u2014then back to the action.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you like games that are <strong>simple to play, hard to put down</strong>, Amulet aims right at that sweet spot: elegant input, readable challenge, and a steady sense of \u201cI\u2019m stronger than I was five minutes ago.\u201d</p>","developers":["Flipside Games"],"genres":[{"description":"Action","id":"1"},{"description":"Indie","id":"23"},{"description":"RPG","id":"3"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2784910/5d697eebd49cbad52196c894598c1387c101fd12/header.jpg?t=1760564551","is_free":false,"linux_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>"},"mac_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>"},"movies":[{"dash_av1":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/2784910/584811481/4c0e9fc7d38e9156e3c28ac49b1ef3681da63b8e/1759894118/dash_av1.mpd?t=1759907580","dash_h264":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/2784910/584811481/4c0e9fc7d38e9156e3c28ac49b1ef3681da63b8e/1759894118/dash_h264.mpd?t=1759907580","highlight":true,"hls_h264":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/2784910/584811481/4c0e9fc7d38e9156e3c28ac49b1ef3681da63b